WEBVTT

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:28.000
We've received a report that a dead etemohn 
has been discovered in the forest.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:31.520
Gashita!

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:36.470
Because you kept dawdling, 
Dariel defeated it in your place!

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.040
You should make sure to thank Dariel.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.220
<i>There's no need to tell him that.</i>

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:45.920
Thank you very much.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.520
<i>See? I knew it would turn out like this.</i>

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.750
Stop that! That's...

00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:58.700
Looking for medicinal herbs, huh?

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.580
That's fitting work for an E-rank.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:03.520
Just watch!

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:07.100
I'm better than some 
novice geezer, and I'll prove it!

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:10.650
Oh, dear...

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:12.630
I'll be going too.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:14.800
Oh, just a moment, Dariel.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:22.570
Hot!

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.650
Under the aegis of the god of battle, 
 your rank has been raised.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:32.620
You did defeat the etemohn and 
protect the village, after all.

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:35.400
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:37.910
Let's do our best together!

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.660
It isn't necessary for you to 
accompany me on my quests too.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:43.860
Oh, it's fine!

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:48.290
Mister Dariel, you've only 
just arrived in the village!

00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:51.930
You need someone to show you around!

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:53.900
<i>She overruled me...</i>

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:14.690
<b>Chillin'</b>

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:14.690
<b>in My 30s after Getting Fired from the Demon King's Army</b>

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:32.030
Um, Miss Malika?

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:34.020
You don't need to do all of this for me.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:38.030
The forest is dangerous. That's why 
people hire adventurers, isn't it?

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:42.530
Don't worry! Villagers go into the forest, too.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:47.090
We ask adventurers to do things like 
go into the depths of the forest

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:49.280
or to dangerous areas.

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:50.540
And also...

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:53.120
when we're too lazy to go ourselves.

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:57.130
<i>Could it be that adventuring work
is just about doing odd jobs?</i>

00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:00.130
<b>Episode 2</b>

00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:00.130
<b>Dariel Works His First Assignment
 as an Adventurer.</b>

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:05.550
Oh! It's been a long time 
since I climbed this.

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:09.720
Will you be all right?

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:15.730
Yes! I wanted to be an adventurer too.

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:18.430
I wanted to be of help to the village.

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:19.230
Is that why...

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:21.490
you were in the forest back then?

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:29.750
Yes. An old lady in my neighborhood 
had a cold coming on.

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:30.330
But...

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:34.330
That idiot Gashita wouldn't go 
pick any medicinal herbs for us.

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:38.340
So, I had no choice... but to go myself.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:43.070
Truly, you don't need to go this far for me.

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:43.590
What?

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:48.300
Today, I wanted to repay you for saving me.

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:51.580
So, please, overlook it for today.

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:52.600
Yes.

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:55.870
I have already over...looked at quite a lot.

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:58.110
Mister Dariel,

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:02.110
let's hold hands!

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:03.860
What? Why?

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:06.030
So that we don't get separated.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:08.620
Isn't there any other way to prevent that?

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.100
Then shall we embrace?

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:12.250
No, thank you.

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:27.380
We're here!

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:33.260
Well, then, let's finish this up all at once!

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:34.640
A-All right.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:39.020
This is the medicinal herb 
we're gathering this time.

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:46.680
<i>Miss Malika...</i>

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:48.910
<i>She seems very used to doing an 
adventurer's work, doesn't she?</i>

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:53.540
Oh.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.640
That isn't hurtsbeyondbe leaf.

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:56.270
What?

00:05:56.920 --> 00:06:01.300
Hurtsbeyondbe leaf is jagged 
around the edges, like this.

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:05.840
Also, please only take one leaf.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.230
That way it can be harvested again.

00:06:08.230 --> 00:06:09.480
I see.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:10.990
Thank you.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:13.730
While we're at it...

00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:15.600
let's pick some bloodstaunch herb, too!

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:17.770
If I'm remembering right...

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:19.220
It should be around... here.

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:22.610
There! I found it!

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:27.680
Oh! Look!

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:30.160
Deer tracks!

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:33.870
Where?

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:37.120
Let's track it and bring it down.

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:39.640
And then we can have it for dinner tonight!

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:42.990
<i>I'd expect no less of the daughter 
of the guild master and mayor.</i>

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:44.100
<i>She's quite robust.</i>

00:06:44.660 --> 00:06:46.880
Um... Miss Malika?

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:49.200
I thought this back with the monkey, too.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.500
Couldn't you have managed by yourself?

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:54.680
No, I couldn't have.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.890
I'm scared to fight.

00:06:57.920 --> 00:06:59.200
That's why...

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:03.460
Mister Dariel, you are my savior.

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:11.000
And I have a favor to ask 
of my honorable savior.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:13.160
What is it, Miss Malika?

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:15.710
U-Um...

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:21.080
I wish you wouldn't call me "Miss" Malika.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:21.920
What?

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:26.630
I think it's time... for you 
to call me just by my name.

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:29.580
Using "Miss" makes it seem like 
we're strangers, doesn't it?

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:32.920
<i>Well, the fact is that we 
pretty much </i>are<i> strangers.</i>

00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:35.180
Please, Mister Dariel!

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:37.730
M...

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:39.930
M...

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:43.270
M...iss Malika.

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:46.170
Oh! You are such a meanie!

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:48.000
Mister Dariel!

00:07:48.670 --> 00:07:49.510
A deer!

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:50.780
What? Where?

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:54.740
Mister Dariel, you're amazing!

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.030
<i>There really was one there!</i>

00:07:58.570 --> 00:08:02.160
<i>Well, it's got a cute little face.</i>

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:03.550
<i>Huh?</i>

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:09.300
Watch out!

00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:19.810
<i>That monster and the deer are fighting.</i>

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:22.150
<i>What is going on here?</i>

00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:24.950
<i>And the deer is the stronger one!</i>

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:26.230
Since we have the opportunity...

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:28.670
Let's take them both down.

00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:30.080
They look so delicious!

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:30.690
<i>What?</i>

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:40.770
The deer and the monster...

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:43.420
Mister Dariel hunted both 
of them down for us.

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:46.720
But he was on an herb-gathering quest!

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:48.170
He's incredible.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:51.170
Oh, no, not at all.

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:54.610
Oh. Gashita.

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:00.970
<i>Huh?</i>

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:09.230
<i>Oh, dear!</i>

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:12.880
<i>This has become even more of a mess.</i>

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:19.370
<i>And so...</i>

00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:21.330
<i>the days passed.</i>

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:24.500
<i>I've become used to life here.</i>

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:30.720
<i>In general, my time here 
passes without incident.</i>

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:43.300
Tch!

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:58.110
<i>This sort of thing does stress
 me out a little, though.</i>

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:01.120
Welcome home!

00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:02.930
Would you like your meal?

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:04.420
Would you like to use the sauna?

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:06.210
Or, would you like...

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:07.360
Sir.

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:09.210
Father?

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:11.630
I've completed the gathering quest.

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:15.180
Is something wrong?

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:17.500
Oh, you're back.

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:20.890
It's just that Gashita 
is a little out of control.

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:25.270
After all, he's had his targets 
taken by you twice, Dariel.

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:26.310
Yes...

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:28.140
I do feel bad about that.

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:31.660
Mister Dariel, you haven't 
done anything wrong!

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:34.400
Hunting monsters when you have the chance 
is good sense and common practice!

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:36.000
That it is.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:39.400
By rights, adventurers in the same 
guild should be working together.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:44.410
Oh, but it's something else that 
I'm worried about right now.

00:10:47.730 --> 00:10:50.500
When Gashita was in here just now,

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:53.420
this arrived as an urgent request.

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:56.440
It's limited to C-rank and above...

00:10:56.440 --> 00:10:58.400
a blaze deathscythe.

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:02.430
It's a far more dangerous monster 
than the etemohn or the antrassic.

00:11:02.860 --> 00:11:05.930
<i>What is with this excessively 
powerful looking thing?</i>

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:13.440
But this monster should be handled by the 
guild from a bigger town, shouldn't it?

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:15.450
Exactly.

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:18.780
The quest to defeat it is meant for those 
C-ranked and above in the next town over.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:21.910
It was sent to us just so we'd know to be on guard.

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:25.180
And that's how Gashita ended up seeing it?

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:27.870
Honestly, how many times is this now?

00:11:29.150 --> 00:11:32.810
Being guild master and mayor 
at the same time is exhausting.

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:36.130
<i>Miss Malika is relentless 
with members of her family.</i>

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:36.130
You need to be more careful, Father!

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:37.420
Um...

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:40.270
Is it all right to be this relaxed?

00:11:40.270 --> 00:11:43.240
If the monster is a C-rank and above target,

00:11:43.240 --> 00:11:46.500
then won't it be bad for Gashita 
to fight it, since he's D-ranked?

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:48.640
Oh, that won't be a problem.

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:49.350
What?

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:55.860
The guild from the neighboring town has 
already formed a large cordon to deal with it.

00:11:56.210 --> 00:11:57.110
Well, then.

00:11:57.110 --> 00:12:01.750
But is it all right for our adventurers 
to invade another party's area?

00:12:01.750 --> 00:12:02.360
Oh.

00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:06.160
If that happened, wouldn't the 
issue become your responsibility?

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:07.090
Uh-oh!

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:09.620
I'll go.

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:12.080
I'll bring Gashita back.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:13.230
Oh!

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:14.560
Then, I'll go too.

00:12:14.560 --> 00:12:16.670
No, this time I'll go alone.

00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:18.670
But...

00:12:19.020 --> 00:12:22.400
You leave the dangerous things 
to the adventurers, don't you?

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:26.760
All right.

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:29.170
I'll go get your things ready.

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:33.230
Please take these.

00:12:34.510 --> 00:12:37.640
They're medicines made with the 
herbs we gathered together.

00:12:37.640 --> 00:12:38.690
Thank you.

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:41.000
Well, then...

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:44.420
I'll be off.

00:12:54.690 --> 00:12:56.110
<i>It seems like rain.</i>

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:06.200
<i>I feel a sense of uneasiness.</i>

00:13:06.910 --> 00:13:08.580
<i>From my time in the Demon King's Army,</i>

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:11.970
<i>I know that whenever I ignore 
this feeling, I always regret it.</i>

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:14.200
<i>I must do everything in my power to...</i>

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:25.210
Th-This is...

00:13:31.230 --> 00:13:33.870
What are the people in 
that giant cordon doing?

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:48.340
<i>This time...</i>

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:50.780
<i>putting my life on the line...</i>

00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:53.600
<i>seems like it will be necessary!</i>

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:58.060
<b>Chillin'
 in My 30s after Getting Fired from the Demon King's Army</b>

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:01.780
Stay away!

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:02.970
Stay away!

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:05.940
Stay away!

00:14:07.520 --> 00:14:09.200
<i>A blaze deathscythe.</i>

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:13.410
<i>It's on a completely different level 
from anything I've fought up to now.</i>

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:14.950
<i>If I lose focus, it'll be over in an instant!</i>

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:23.710
<i>It's targeting Gashita?</i>

00:14:25.060 --> 00:14:25.910
This is bad!

00:14:26.850 --> 00:14:27.550
Blast it!

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:32.050
Don't underestimate the number 
one adventurer in the village!

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:34.810
<i>How can it be so tough?</i>

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:47.150
What? That's so much Aura!

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:49.150
Slice through!

00:14:55.840 --> 00:14:57.270
Was that too shallow?

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:13.600
<i>My weapon!</i>

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:22.100
<i>If I want to shatter something,</i>

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:23.610
<b>HIT</b>

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:23.610
<b>HIT</b>

00:15:22.720 --> 00:15:23.610
<i>then use Hit!</i>

00:15:24.580 --> 00:15:25.610
<i>If I'm throwing...</i>

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:27.110
<b>STING</b>

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:27.110
<b>STING</b>

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:27.110
<i>then use Sting!</i>

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:29.610
<i>One of them is the right answer!</i>

00:15:30.520 --> 00:15:31.280
<i>No.</i>

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:34.670
<i>It's both!</i>

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:12.140
Glad that worked out somehow.

00:16:20.140 --> 00:16:21.490
Were you bitten?

00:16:21.490 --> 00:16:22.410
Yes.

00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:25.590
It's hurting more and more.

00:16:26.090 --> 00:16:27.920
Was that thing poisonous?

00:16:28.240 --> 00:16:29.690
A-Am I...

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:32.770
g-going to die?

00:16:32.770 --> 00:16:34.180
Don't worry.

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:36.430
We have antivenom.

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:39.600
Miss Malika made sure that I brought it.

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:42.320
She knew just from looking 
at the wanted poster...

00:16:42.320 --> 00:16:44.540
that the monster would be poisonous.

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:47.550
It's bitter!

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:51.360
W-Will I live?

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:52.400
We'll figure something out.

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:02.540
Th-That hurts!

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:04.860
Bear with it. It's bloodstaunch herb.

00:17:11.690 --> 00:17:14.520
How do you know so much about it?

00:17:14.520 --> 00:17:17.510
I studied while doing the 
medicinal herb gathering quest.

00:17:19.020 --> 00:17:21.830
This medicine was made using those herbs.

00:17:21.830 --> 00:17:24.930
I learned about bloodstaunch 
herb from Miss Malika, too.

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:34.180
It isn't all the time, but... I can feel it.

00:17:35.590 --> 00:17:37.110
And then I realize...

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:40.620
everything is connected.

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:44.620
There isn't anything in this 
world that's pointless.

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:57.180
And with that, we should be safe for now.

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:04.060
<i>Still...</i>

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:04.890
Damn it!

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:07.660
<i>This boy certainly does cry a lot.</i>

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:19.850
Well, this is a luxurious start to the day.

00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:22.990
There's still a lot of meat 
left from the deer yesterday.

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:26.860
Mister Dariel, please eat 
lots and lots, all right?

00:18:26.860 --> 00:18:29.450
Th-Thank you.

00:18:32.660 --> 00:18:35.460
Good morning, Big Bro!

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:38.350
Big Bro?

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:40.540
What happened between you?

00:18:41.750 --> 00:18:44.900
I happened to realize...

00:18:44.900 --> 00:18:48.180
that there's nothing in this 
world that's pointless.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:51.190
That's the thing I said yesterday.

00:18:51.470 --> 00:18:54.580
Whatever the case! I owe Big Bro my life!

00:18:54.580 --> 00:18:58.190
I want to heal as quickly as I 
can and work under my big bro!

00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:01.920
I like that attitude, but Mister 
Dariel is busy right now.

00:18:59.010 --> 00:19:02.700
<i>I'm technically the junior here, though.</i>

00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:04.370
Go home immediately and focus on healing!

00:19:03.270 --> 00:19:07.700
<i>Not long ago, I was just a failure who'd 
been cut loose from the Demon King's Army.</i>

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:07.700
Thanks to Big Bro, 
my wounds are already better!

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:09.200
<i>Speaking of which,</i>

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:14.380
<i>I wonder if the Four Generals 
are still fighting the hero.</i>

00:19:20.270 --> 00:19:20.970
And?

00:19:21.310 --> 00:19:27.470
Zebiantes, as a result, you shamelessly 
fled from the hero's party?

00:19:27.470 --> 00:19:29.980
As I said!

00:19:30.320 --> 00:19:34.730
No one told me anything about the 
hero's party gaining new members!

00:19:35.120 --> 00:19:38.230
Everything that gave my magnificent, 
powerful self trouble

00:19:38.770 --> 00:19:41.990
is the fault of their new spearman!

00:19:42.310 --> 00:19:43.950
Then, I ask you...

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:48.460
Why were you unable to gain word 
of this spearman beforehand?

00:19:50.480 --> 00:19:54.250
Scouting prior to battle is 
the most basic of basics.

00:19:54.550 --> 00:19:56.840
Th-That's...

00:19:56.840 --> 00:19:58.520
all his fault!

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:02.960
It's all because the assistant to the Four 
Generals was negligent in his scouting!

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:03.790
You!

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:07.510
You're fired.

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:08.920
Get out of my sight.

00:20:12.420 --> 00:20:15.120
Now we must once again 
select a new assistant.

00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:18.360
They're all so incompetent.
 I'm getting sick of the whole thing.

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:22.030
We've already had four or 
five of them, haven't we?

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:24.820
Wouldn't it be best to bring him back?

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:25.530
What?

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:29.040
Doroye, what are you trying to say?

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:32.790
Our first assistant... Dariel.

00:20:34.980 --> 00:20:38.480
He always executed his work perfectly,

00:20:38.480 --> 00:20:40.090
he was skilled in tactics,

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:43.690
and he even took care in 
looking after our health.

00:20:51.200 --> 00:20:55.100
As I am of the moon, there are times 
when even walking demands great effort.

00:20:55.410 --> 00:20:59.320
In those times, he would help me without 
those around us noticing anything.

00:21:06.880 --> 00:21:09.280
After losing him, I realized 
for the first time...

00:21:09.640 --> 00:21:12.790
that we need his strength.

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:15.140
For the victory of the Demon King's Army...

00:21:15.140 --> 00:21:17.790
isn't it the best course of 
action to bring Dariel back?

00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:19.980
Th...

00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:21.590
Th...

00:21:22.350 --> 00:21:24.720
That deeply unpleasant name...

00:21:25.290 --> 00:21:28.810
Do not ever say it!

00:21:28.810 --> 00:21:29.720
Hold on!

00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:31.470
Bashbarza, stop!

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:33.020
It's so hot!

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:36.730
I will never let that happen!

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:40.310
Mister Dariel, do you have a cold?

00:21:40.310 --> 00:21:42.240
No, it's nothing.

00:21:41.530 --> 00:21:42.970
Big Bro!

00:21:42.970 --> 00:21:45.740
This is really good! Please have some!

00:21:45.740 --> 00:21:48.000
I gave him some of that just now!

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:50.800
Does that matter? It's a second helping!

00:21:50.800 --> 00:21:53.700
Mister Dariel can't eat that much!

00:21:52.360 --> 00:21:53.700
<i>After getting fired...</i>

00:21:54.090 --> 00:21:57.230
<i>as I wandered, I happened 
to arrive in this village.</i>

00:21:57.840 --> 00:22:00.890
<i>But gradually, it's becoming 
a new hometown for me.</i>

00:22:02.240 --> 00:22:05.820
<i>I hope that the Four Generals 
are doing well too.</i>

00:23:41.650 --> 00:23:46.170
Next time on <i>Chillin' in My 30s After 
Getting Fired from the Demon King's Army</i>...

00:23:46.170 --> 00:23:48.780
"Dariel Goes to His Old Workplace."

00:23:48.780 --> 00:23:51.070
<b>Episode 3</b>

00:23:48.780 --> 00:23:51.070
<b>Dariel Goes to His Old Workplace.</b>
